  "repo_truth": "Review 4 admitted the exact 24-path subject and returned one Required rollback-destination collision gap plus one Nit stale-source citation gap. The parent accepted both without waiver. This exact 25-path subject defines independent four-state committed and rolled-back destination axes, permits only absent destinations to rename, refuses/preserves every collision/unsafe/simultaneous suffix, and adds symmetric negatives/plan/checklist assertions. The research note now cites immutable pre-repair commit cfd954c and its exact Review 6 manifest instead of mutable line meanings. Intent 1.2, identity values, fsync and scratch repairs, verified snapshot, Rust scope, and HCM-2.3 stop are unchanged.",
  "allowed_scope": ["Remain read-only and replay all 25 manifest hashes/order/aggregate before review.", "Independently review the entire complete identity/currentness/persistence/recovery subject, not only Review 4 repairs.", "Adversarially verify both four-state terminal destination axes and negatives, terminal-marker fsync replay, immutable research support, transaction-keyed journals, whole-file scratch publication, 36+8 fault products, W0-W15/R0-R9, collision and mismatch preservation.", "Return findings first with exact evidence, failure mode, smallest repair, and missing validation."],
  "non_goals": ["No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, snapshot mutation, or user task hops.", "No Rust/test work, implementation resumption, schema widening, fallback/dual read, relaxed validation, prior-evidence rewrite, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.", "Do not inherit prior verdicts; derive the whole result independently."],
  "tasks": ["Invoke ordered skills and return BLOCKED on any manifest mismatch.", "Verify the complete identity graph, schemas/vectors, source support, persistence, currentness, writer/recovery, collisions, mismatch, fsync, and fault grammar.", "Prove only absent terminal destinations rename for both outcomes; every collision preserves pending; all whole-file/fsync/path/fault rules remain complete and scratch never enters recovery.", "Return CLEAN only with no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding; otherwise CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repair."],
